# Candidate run state: progress, scoreboard, timer, terminal transcripts, the
# no-AI acknowledgement, input-guard flags, editor save records and archived
# runs. Ignored as a whole directory rather than file by file — this list was
# enumerated once and then silently fell behind every time a new piece of state
# was added, which is how a real candidate's transcript ends up one `git add -A`
# from a public repo. Nothing under state/ is ever meant to be committed; it is
# runtime data, and deploy.sh already excludes it from the rsync.
state/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env.local
# .env holds CONTROLLER_SECRET on a deployed box and HOST_PORT locally. Only
# .env.local was listed, so the real one was committable.
.env

# basic-auth secrets (generated by ./gen-auth.sh) — never commit
nginx/auth/htpasswd
nginx/auth/htpasswd-interviewer

# SSH keys never belong in here. deploy.sh rsyncs this whole directory to the
# server, so a stray .pem would be copied to the box as well.
*.pem
*.key

# Local Claude Code settings (machine-specific, and they can capture command
# arguments verbatim, including passwords typed into a shell).
.claude/

# The employees sample database is fetched, not committed (~34 MB).
# build.sh calls tools/fetch-employees.sh when it is missing.
exercises/_base/employees-db.tar.gz
exercises/*/employees-db.tar.gz

# The written answer key is kept outside this public repo.
/SOLUTIONS.md
